  "scope": "Repair purchased-hardware axial retention without changing any printed part. Add four large stock M3 clearance washers to the existing M2 journal stacks, retain all eight small M2 washers, move the inner small washers/nuts inward by 0.8 mm, and use the motor drawing maximum diameter of 13.6 mm instead of nominal 13.5 mm.",
  "mechanical_basis": {
    "defect": "The old OD5 mm inner washer and M2 nut could pass through the carrier D-hole; sleeve retention was not established by an overlap with a corner of the hex nut.",
    "correction": "Four DIN9021/ISO7093-1 SUS304 3.2x9x0.8 mm unthreaded retainers engage the carrier D-flat. Keep the 2.2x5x0.3 mm small washer between each retainer and M2 nut: the M3 bore maximum3.38 mm exceeds the M2 minimum chamfered bearing diameter3.2 mm.",
    "drawing_sources": {
      "large_washer": "https://www.jcfasteners.com/wp-content/uploads/DIN-9021-Large-Washer-B4D03-SS304.pdf",
      "small_washer": "https://www.jcfasteners.com/wp-content/uploads/DIN-125-Plain-Washer-B4D02-SS304.pdf",
      "nut_bearing_diameter": "https://eshop.boellhoff.de/out/media/pdf/DIN_934_Edelstahl_A2___en.pdf",
      "motor": "https://www.happymodel.cn/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/RS1102-KV10000.jpg"
    },
    "qualification_limit": "Nominal and tolerance geometry are screening only. Selected supplier lots, eccentric seating, clamp preload, PA12 creep, bearing strength and vibration retention remain unqualified."
  },
